  "details": "Full body tracking can be such a pain because you have an unstable bluetooth connection of 5 devices plus possibly a wireless HMD. If one of those fails, you will have to restart VRChat because if you just restart the device, it's new ID after restart will mess everything up (your hip becomes a controller etc.)\n\nBest solution: \n- allow us to assign static devices in the menu to a certain position of our body (see source code below) to always have the same vive tracker as for example our hip tracker at the hip etc. If my headset crashes, don't randomly treat my tracker as a controller, wait for my real controller to reconnect instead. The game then knows what a tracker is, where it is supposed to be and doesn't need to use dynamic device IDs for it anymore. Currently, full  body tracking is just a pain because of this dynamic device ID mess.\n\nAnother solution:\n- at the first rigging process, the game knows how many trackers are in use. If this number decreases, temporary treat the two controllers at the highest point in the room as the hands to avoid that the trackers turn into controllers (very annoying bug currently).\n- ask the user to re-rigg again, in case he wanted to decrease the trackers (very unlikely). He can then turn them all on again but will screw up the device ID order. So he needs to re-rigg anyway\n- also allow user to re-rigg on demand\n- in a T-pose rigg, the game knows where the left hand, right hand and each tracker is, simply by the relative position and height to each other and the HMD direction facing forward. The device ID should be completely irrelevant and also the old position in the lates rigging process. It should also be possible to turn on more controllers during that rigging process.\n\n(Source code by BOLL):\nuint index = [whichever device you want to check]; ETrackedPropertyError error = new ETrackedPropertyError(); StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(); OpenVR.System.GetStringTrackedDeviceProperty(index, ETrackedDeviceProperty.Prop_SerialNumber_String, sb, OpenVR.k_unMaxPropertyStringSize, ref error); var probablyUniqueDeviceSerial = sb.ToString();",
